# Node self-deregistration key — forced-command, root login restricted to ONE action.
#
# This is the "permission to delete a node" half (the SSH key's matching authorized_keys entry).
# The `command="..."` forces every login with this key to run ONLY the delete wrapper, ignoring
# whatever the client asks for; `restrict` disables port/agent/X11 forwarding, pty, etc. So even
# though it logs in as root, a leaked key can do exactly one thing: delete the Node object whose
# name the client passes. This is why no separate sudoers rule is needed.
#
# DUMMY KEY committed below — replace with the REAL public key at bake time:
#   ~/hami-cluster-test/deregister-keys/id_ed25519.pub   (private half goes on the nodes at
#   /etc/rke2-deregister/id_ed25519 via the common overlay).
command="/usr/local/sbin/deregister-node.sh",restrict ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIOyPveRoVPq5GpcKRCmoA1IY3qaRbSPqdbnf91JGL6rP DUMMY-aleph-node-deregister-REPLACE-AT-BAKE
